# The project's quality tiers — the numeric sub-knobs behind the frame document's
# one-word `quality:`. Guide: docs/guide/rendering/render-quality.
#
# The waterfall folds per parameter: engine defaults, then this file, then a `preset:`
# inline on the !StandardFrame node itself. A tier names only what it overrides and an
# unset field falls through, so an empty file — this one — inherits the whole engine
# table. The host hands it over at registration:
#
#     config.Graphics.Factories.Add(new PostEffectFactory { Preset = loadedPreset });
#
# Uncomment to start overriding. Every entry maps to a named engine knob:
#
# high: !QualityTierOverrides
#   shadows: !ShadowQuality { cascadeResolution: 4096 }
# low: !QualityTierOverrides
#   resolution: !ResolutionQuality { renderScale: 0.75 }
